  hp_acases_t: 'Case studies', hp_acases_s: 'Content → Cases',
  hp_acases_1: 'The “Cases” tab → “New case”. Write down what happened, what was done, the outcome, what went wrong and what it teaches.',
  hp_acases_2: 'The “Fill in with AI” button turns a short note into a full case — check the facts before you save.',
  hp_acases_3: 'Link the standards by hand or with the automatic button — the case then appears at the bottom of the matching lesson.',
  hp_acases_4: 'A draft is visible only to you. After “Publish” the case appears for employees and the case mentor starts answering from it.',
  hp_abase_t: 'Journals and terminology', hp_abase_s: 'Content → Journals / Terminology',
  hp_abase_1: 'The “Journals” tab → “New journal”: the name, what it is for, then the columns — text, number, date, a pick from a list, or an employee.',
  hp_abase_2: 'The “Who can see it” block: all employees, permanent staff only, or selected people — by department, position, minimum level and by name. Right beside it you see how many people that comes to.',
  hp_abase_3: 'Separately, “Who can add rows”: you only, or everyone who can see the journal.',
  hp_abase_4: 'Attach template files — blank forms and memos the employee downloads straight from the journal.',
  hp_abase_5: 'The “Terminology” tab: terms show up in the glossary and the AI mentor uses them in its answers. Each term card has a block for the Chinese translation.',
  hp_aquality_t: 'Work quality', hp_aquality_s: 'Mistakes, trainer, acknowledgements',
  hp_aquality_1: 'The “Quality” section, “Mistakes” tab: log what happened and link the standard.',
  hp_aquality_2: 'The system assigns the employee a re-read and a mini test on its own; the list shows who has already put it right.',
  hp_aquality_3: 'The “Trainer” tab shows how employees do in the AI scenarios and their scores by criterion: standard, tone, completeness, safety.',
  hp_aquality_4: 'The “Acknowledgements” tab shows who has not yet confirmed reading the updated standard.',
  hp_alevels_t: 'Setting up levels', hp_alevels_s: 'The career ladder',
  hp_alevels_1: 'The “Levels” section: for every step set the XP threshold, the required sections, the minimum average score and the number of accepted initiatives.',
  hp_alevels_2: 'In the “Names and description” block you edit the name, the caption, the “what has to grow” requirements and the benefits — in all four languages.',
  hp_alevels_3: 'The “Preview celebration” button plays the promotion screen — handy for checking what the employee will see.',
  hp_alevels_4: 'After “Save” the changes show up for employees straight away in the “My path” tab and on the career ladder.',
  hp_aassets_t: 'Property and feedback', hp_aassets_s: 'Property and Feedback',
  hp_aassets_1: 'The “Property” section: what has been issued, what the employee declared themselves and where there is a mismatch. The number in the menu is how many items need you.',
  hp_aassets_2: 'Confirm an issue, correct a mismatch or mark a return — the employee sees the change on their side.',
  hp_aassets_3: 'The “Feedback” section: employee initiatives and pulse survey results. Reply — the status and the reply are visible to the author.',
  hp_aassets_4: 'The AI assistant (the button at the bottom right) can pull together a summary of mood and initiatives: just ask it in your own words.',

  tip_home_t: 'Home', tip_home: 'Your current lesson, today’s tasks and your progress. The “Continue” button opens where you left off.',
  tip_tasks_t: 'Tasks', tip_tasks: 'Everything that needs action from you: read an updated standard, or re-train after a mistake.',
  tip_cases_t: 'Cases', tip_cases: 'Real situations from the company’s work. Describe your situation to the case mentor — it finds a similar one and tells you what was done then.',
  tip_base_t: 'Base', tip_base: 'Company journals and the glossary of terms. You see only what the methodologist opened; where it is allowed, you can add rows.',
  tip_path_t: 'My path', tip_path: 'Your level, XP and the requirements for the next step. Hover over a level and we show the requirements and the benefits.',
  tip_assets_t: 'My property', tip_assets: 'Check the list of what was issued. Report a breakage, or say an item was never issued to you — the request goes to the methodologist.',
  tip_ideas_t: 'My initiatives', tip_ideas: 'The ideas and problems you have sent, and management’s replies. Send a new one with the red button at the top.',
  tip_drill_t: 'AI trainer', tip_drill: 'Pick a scenario and answer as you would in real life: the AI plays a client or an inspector, and scores you against the criteria at the end.',
  tip_inbox_t: 'Requests', tip_inbox: 'Employee questions, exam requests, access requests and promotion requests. A dot on the left means unread.',
  tip_monitor_t: 'Monitoring', tip_monitor: 'How everyone is getting on: lessons passed, average score, study time, who is behind schedule.',
  tip_quality_t: 'Quality', tip_quality: 'The mistake log with automatic re-reading, the AI trainer results and acknowledgements of updated standards.',
  tip_cms_t: 'Content', tip_cms: 'Lessons, cases, journals and terminology. This is also where you set who sees what and who may add rows.',
  tip_staff_t: 'Employees', tip_staff: 'Add an employee, issue access, change status and level. The list is grouped by level, and the “Survey” column shows mood.',
  tip_levels_t: 'Levels', tip_levels: 'The career ladder: XP thresholds, required sections and the requirements for every step, in four languages.',
  tip_aassets_t: 'Property', tip_aassets: 'What has been issued to employees, what they declared themselves and where the mismatches are. Anything needing action is flagged by the number in the menu.',
  tip_feedback_t: 'Feedback', tip_feedback: 'Employee initiatives and pulse survey results. A reply to an initiative is visible to its author.'
